# arsenal-catalog -- one-line description per tool, joined by `arsenal` into a
# human menu. name<TAB>description. rides p3 (capability), so adding a tool means
# a line here + a rebuild, never an image change. keep lowercase + terse.
ffuf	web fuzzer -- brute paths/params/vhosts against a target
httpx	fast http prober -- which hosts/ports actually answer, titles, tech
nuclei	template-driven vuln + misconfig scanner
subfinder	passive subdomain discovery
dnsx	fast dns toolkit -- resolve, bruteforce, record types
gobuster	dir/dns/vhost brute-forcer
chisel	tcp/udp tunnel over http -- pivot / port-forward through a firewall
socat	swiss-army socket relay -- pivot, port-forward, tls-wrap, listen
ligolo-proxy	pivot -- operator-side proxy for ligolo-ng tun tunnels
ligolo-agent	pivot -- target-side agent for ligolo-ng, dropped on a foothold
masscan	internet-scale port scanner (fast, stateless)
nmap	host/service/version/os scan + nse scripting -- what masscan can't
tcpdump	packet capture + inspection on the wire
links	text-mode web browser -- reads served zims and any html/http, no gui
python	full cpython 3.12 -- scripting, a repl, http.server, the swiss knife
sqlmap	automated sql-injection detection + exploitation
impacket	windows/ad attack suite -- secretsdump, ntlmrelayx, psexec, kerberos (70 tools)
mutool	pdf reader (mupdf) -- `draw -F txt|html` turns any pdf into readable text
kiwix-serve	serve offline zims (wikipedia, survival docs) on localhost for links
kiwix-search	grep the zims from the cli without a server
frotz	z-machine interpreter -- plays the if/ interactive-fiction story files
whois	who registered this domain/ip -- the one basic busybox doesn't ship
hydra	online service login brute-forcer (ssh/http/ftp/...)
john	offline password hash cracker (bleeding-jumbo, cpu-only)
pspy	watch processes/cron without root -- local privesc enumeration
jq	json parser/filter -- for the json every other tool here emits
rg	ripgrep -- fast search over the staged corpora and loot
zstd	decompress .zst images/firmware/payloads nothing else here reads
ddrescue	image a dying disk -- copy what reads, log the bad ranges, resume
strace	trace a binary's syscalls -- files, connections, why it exits
testdisk	rebuild a lost or corrupt partition table and its boot sectors
photorec	carve files back off a formatted or damaged filesystem by signature
smartctl	read a drive's SMART health -- is it dying before you trust or wipe it
file	identify an unknown blob by content -- where strings only shows text
mandoc	render a man page -- the reader for the staged man-pages corpus, no roff
binwalk	scan a firmware blob for embedded filesystems, keys and streams
cc	compile C on the stick -- tcc (its own cpp/as/linker), static, + a musl sysroot
radare2	reverse-engineer a binary offline -- disassemble, analyse, hex-edit (r2/rabin2/rax2)
minisign	sign/verify a file -- ed25519, one binary, no gpg trust model
age	encrypt/decrypt a file -- modern, no gpg keyring, passphrase or keypair
dvtm	suckless terminal multiplexer -- split panes, no server, no config
rsync	sync/backup over ssh -- delta transfer, resumable
atlas	offline vector atlas -- renders natural-earth maps as characters, braille to ascii, on any terminal
view	image/pdf viewer -- renders any picture or pdf page as characters, braille to ascii, via mutool
